        <mxCell id="c35" value="&lt;i&gt;Each bar starts at zero, in its own scale. The straight-time rate barely moved ($26.57, $26.59, $26.62 an hour), so the rise in the cost of a labor hour is the overtime premium on a growing overtime share (11.6%, 16.7%, 19.8%). The hours per standard hour rose 28.0%, the cost of an hour 4.1%, and their product 33.2%: 1.280 × 1.041 = 1.332.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="284" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
